\title{Finite sets are countable}
\date{2026-03-12T13:56:02Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Remark}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Clearly every finite set is [countable](00AT), since we can match up the elements of a finite set with, say, some finite prefix of the natural numbers #{\{0, 1, 2, 3, \dots, n\}}.}

##{\begin{array}{ccccccc}
  A: & a_0 & a_1 & a_2 & a_3 & \dots & a_n \\
    & \updownarrow& \updownarrow& \updownarrow& \updownarrow& \updownarrow& \updownarrow \\
  \N: & 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 & \dots & n
\end{array}}

\transclude{00AW}
